instruction: Given the aforementioned set of integer elements, construct a JavaScript code fragment that is specifically designed to segregate and retrieve items that exhibit a numerical value exceeding the threshold of 10.
arr = [2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 18];
response:
Here is a piece of JavaScript code using the `filter` function to retrieve the elements of the array that are greater than 10.

```js
var arr = [2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 18];
var res = arr.filter(function(num) {
 return num > 10;
});
console.log(res); // Output: [12, 15, 18]
```

This code first assigns our array to `arr`, then calls `.filter` on `arr`. `.filter` is a method that creates a new array with all elements that pass the test implemented by the provided function. In this case, the test is `num > 10`, so all elements in the input array for which `num > 10` is true will be included in the output.
You could also use arrow functions to make this code more compact:

```js
var arr = [2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 18];
var res = arr.filter(num => num > 10);
console.log(res); // Output: [12, 15, 18]
```

