instruction: Create a Java program that performs matrix operations. 

The program should contain a function `matrixSum` that takes in two 2D arrays (matrices) of size NxM and KxL. If the sizes are not equal (i.e., N is not equal to K or M is not equal to L), the function should print an error message. If the sizes are equal, then your program should add these two matrices together and returns the resulting matrix.

Assume that the matrices will only contain integers. 

Note: 
Matrix addition is performed by adding the corresponding entries together. For example, the sum of two matrices A and B is calculated as follows : A[i][j] + B[i][j]. 

Example:
For matrix A: 
```
A = [[1, 2, 3],
 [4, 5, 6],
 [7, 8, 9]]
```
and matrix B: 
```
B = [[9, 8, 7],
 [6, 5, 4],
 [3, 2, 1]]
```
The sum will be:
```
C = [[10, 10, 10],
 [10, 10, 10],
 [10, 10, 10]]
response:
Here is the Java program that performs the task:

```java
public class Main {

 public static void main(String[] args) {
 int[][] A = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}, {7, 8, 9}};
 int[][] B = {{9, 8, 7}, {6, 5, 4}, {3, 2, 1}};

 int[][] result = matrixSum(A, B);

 if(result != null){
 for(int i=0; i<result.length; i++){
 for(int j=0; j<result[0].length; j++){
 System.out.print(result[i][j] + " ");
 }
 System.out.println();
 }
 }
 }

 public static int[][] matrixSum(int[][] a, int[][] b) {
 if (a.length != b.length || a[0].length != b[0].length) {
 System.out.println("Error: Matrices don't have the same size!");
 return null;
 } else {
 int[][] result = new int[a.length][a[0].length];
 for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
 for (int j = 0; j < a[0].length; j++) {
 result[i][j] = a[i][j] + b[i][j];
 }
 }
 return result;
 }
 }
}
```
In this code, we define two matrices `A` and `B` and calculate their sum with the `matrixSum` method. If the provided matrices do not have the same size, we print an error message and return `null`. Otherwise, we calculate the sum as a new matrix and return it. At the end, we print the resulting matrix if it is not `null`.

Please note that in this code, we assume that all provided matrices are rectangular, i.e., all rows have the same number of columns. In a real-world application, you would probably want to check this assumption before accessing `a[0].length` and `b[0].length`.

