instruction: I am adding custom controls to a FlowLayoutPanel. Each control has a date property. I would like to sort the controls in the flowlayoutpanel based on the date property. I can't presort the controls before I add them because it is possible for the user to add more.

My current thought is when the ControlAdded event for the FlowLayoutPanel is triggered I loop through the controls and use the BringToFront function to order the controls based on the date. 

What is the best way to do this?
response:
Yes, you are correct. When the ControlAdded event fires, you can loop through the controls and sort them. However, using BringToFront will only bring a control to the front of the z-order, not sort all controls.

Here is one approach to sort the FlowLayoutPanel controls by implementing a comparison function:

```csharp
private void SortFlowLayoutPanel()
{
 List<Control> controlList = flowLayoutPanel1.Controls.Cast<Control>().ToList();
 // assuming the 'Date' is a direct property of the control
 controlList.Sort((c1, c2) => ((DateTime)c1.Tag).CompareTo((DateTime)c2.Tag)); 

 flowLayoutPanel1.Controls.Clear(); // clear and re-add in order

 foreach(Control control in controlList)
 {
 flowLayoutPanel1.Controls.Add(control);
 }
}
```

You can call this function in the ControlAdded and ControlRemoved event to maintain the order.

```csharp
private void flowLayoutPanel1_ControlAdded(Object sender, ControlEventArgs e) 
{
 SortFlowLayoutPanel();
}

private void flowLayoutPanel1_ControlRemoved(Object sender, ControlEventArgs e) 
{
 SortFlowLayoutPanel();
}
```

Note that `Tag` property is used to hold the `Date` property for each control. You might need to adjust this according to your implementation.

